papers/116-max-plus-switching-induced-growth/HOSTILE_REVIEW_A.md:274:No credit should be assigned to finite projective Markov reduction as a general method, stationary balance, Poisson martingale CLTs, tilted finite kernels, Perron pressure, Gärtner--Ellis, or switching max-plus terminology. The defensible residual is the arithmetic conjunction for these two matrices: the explicit five-gap quotient, rational drift and variance, cubic, exact support/extremal masses, and temperature constants. That residual remains owner-HOLD pending a broader exact-pair search.
